/* World anchors (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "World anchors"). The runtime
   registers nui-anchor: each frame it places itself on a character's screen
   point (data-attr-vid) by its left and top offset, which moves it without a
   layout or a new mesh, and it stays hidden while the character is not on
   the screen or its own box is not laid out yet.

   <nui-anchor mode="project" height="220" data-attr-vid="sign.vid"/>
   	the character's position raised by height, projected; mode="tail" is
   	its name tail. align-x and align-y pick the point of its own box that
   	sits there (0.5, 0.5: the center); offset-x, offset-y and chat-offset-y
   	add dp.

   Its offsets are screen pixels: put it in a body.nui-overlay, whose box is
   the screen. */

nui-anchor
{
	position: absolute;
	display: block;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
}
